  "id": "restorative-justice",
  "term": "restorative justice",
  "definition": "Restorative justice is an approach to responding to wrongdoing that is presented as an alternative to retributive or punitive justice. Instead of centering on punishment, it is described as a way to address harm without the conflict and added damage associated with excessive reliance on punishment.",
